* AC Analysis of Active Filter (Ideal Op-Amp) - Circuito objetivo
* Sinusoidal Input: Vi = 1mV
* Component Values:
* RA=1.27k, RB=2.3k, G1=1/RA, G2=1/RB
* C1=C2=0.1uF

.PARAM RA_VAL=1.27k
.PARAM RB_VAL=2.3k
.PARAM G1VAL='1/RA_VAL'
.PARAM G2VAL='1/RB_VAL'

V1 1 0 DC 0 AC 1m

* Input Capacitors
C1 1 2 0.1u
C2 2 3 0.1u

* Conductances G1 and G2 (modeladas como resistencias 1/G)
R_G1 2 5 '1/G1VAL'
R_G2 3 0 '1/G2VAL'

* Op-Amp Feedback Network
R_B 5 4 RB_VAL
R_A 4 0 RA_VAL

* Ideal Op-Amp modeled as E-controlled source
E_A1 5 0 3 4 1e6

* 10 Hz a 100 kHz, 4 decadas x 75 = 300 puntos
.AC DEC 75 10 100k

* Print voltages and currents
.PRINT AC V(1) V(2) V(3) V(4) V(5) I(R_B) I(V1)
.PRINT AC VDB(5) VP(5)
.PROBE AC V(1) V(2) V(3) V(4) V(5) I(R_B) I(V1) VDB(5) VP(5)

* POST=2 escribe los resultados en formato ASCII (.ac0 legible)
.OPTION POST=2 PROBE
.OP
.END